                                                "children": [],
                                                "className": "android.widget.TextView",
                                                "text": "Flint's accessibility service detects which app is in the foreground and reads web addresses from known browser address bars for website blocking. While a website rule is active, it re-reads supported browsers' address bars when a page changes. Android also sends page-change signals from other apps; Flint ignores those without reading their content. Address-bar URLs stay in memory; reading stops if Accessibility is off. App and screen class names identify the foreground app. Flint uses this only to enforce the blocks you set up. Everything stays on your device; it is never sent off your device, shared, or sold. Review the full disclosure before choosing whether to open Android Settings.",
